        <body>
            <div xml:id="d17-a3">

                <pb facs="0366" n="356" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv09/pg356"/>

                <head>Appendix C to HD–101</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">drafting
                            committee<lb/>of the conference</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-11-26"
                                ><hi rendition="#small-caps">November</hi> 26,
                        1919</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Note Relative to the Exequatur of
                        Foreign Councils</hi> [<hi rendition="#italic">Consuls</hi>] <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at Danzig</hi></p>
                <p>The Drafting Committee thinks that, during the period from the coming into force
                    of the Peace Treaty with Germany to the definite establishment of a status of
                    the free city of Danzig, the delivery of exequatur will be incumbent upon the
                    representative of the principal Allied and Associated Powers to which the
                    sovereignty is transferred by Article 100 of the said Treaty.</p>
                <closer>For the Drafting Committee<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henri
                            Fromageot</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
